{
  "title": "100: Al-Aadiyaat العاديات",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "There are 11 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. In a tradition from the Holy Prophet (S) it is said that the reward for reciting this Surah is equivalent to ten times the number who are present in ‘Arafah and Muzdalifa at the time of Hajj.\nImam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that those people who recite Surah al-‘Aadiyaat everyday will be counted from the companions of Ameerul Mu’mineen (a.s.) and it has also been narrated that reciting this Surah daily carries the reward of reciting the entire Qur’an. If a person has many creditors, recitation of this Surah will help clear his debts.\nIf recited by a person in fear, this Surah brings him to safety; if recited by a hungry person, it helps in his finding sustenance; if recited by a thirsty person, his thirst will be quenched.\nبِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nوَالْعٰدِيٰتِ ضَبْحًا ۙ‏(1)\nWAL-A’ADEYAATE ZABHAN. \nI swear by the runners breathing pantingly, \nفَالْمُوْرِيٰتِ قَدْحًا ۙ‏(2)\nFAL-MOORE-YAATE QADHAN. \nThen those that produce fire striking, \nفَالْمُغِيْرٰتِ صُبْحًا ۙ‏(3)\nFAL-MOGHEERAATE SUBHAN. \nThen those that make raids at morn, \nفَاَثَرْنَ بِهٖ نَقْعًا ۙ‏(4)\nFA-ASARNA BEHI NAQ-A’N.\nThen thereby raise dust, \nفَوَسَطْنَ بِهٖ جَمْعًا ۙ‏(5)\nFA-WASATNA BEHI JAM-A’N. \nThen rush thereby upon an assembly: \nاِنَّ الْاِنْسَانَ لِرَبِّهٖ لَكَنُوْدٌ ۚ‏(6)\nINNAL INSAANA LE-RABBEHI LA-KANOOD. \nMost surely man is ungrateful to his Lord. \nوَاِنَّهٗ عَلٰى ذٰلِكَ لَشَهِيْدٌ ۚ‏(7)\nWA INNAHU A’LAA ZAALEKA LA-SHAHEED. \nAnd most surely he is a witness of that. \nوَاِنَّهٗ لِحُبِّ الْخَيْرِ لَشَدِيْدٌ ؕ‏(8)\nWA INNAHU LE-HUBBIL KHAYRE LA-SHADEED. \nAnd most surely he is tenacious in the love of wealth. \nاَفَلَا يَعْلَمُ اِذَا بُعْثِرَ مَا فِى الْقُبُوْرِۙ‏(9)\nAFALAA YA’LAMO EZAA BOA’SERA MAA FIL QOBOORE. \nDoes he not then know when what is in the graves is raised, \nوَحُصِّلَ مَا فِى الصُّدُوْرِۙ‏(10)\nWA HUSSELA MAA FIS SODOORE. \nAnd what is in the breasts is made apparent? \nاِنَّ رَبَّهُمْ بِهِمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ لَّخَبِيْرٌ‏(11)\nINNA RABBAHUM BEHIM YAWMA-EZIL LA-KHABEER.\nMost surely their Lord that day shall be fully aware of them. "
}
